# D-PEER-OPEN-UNLINKED-CHAIN-REMOVE-FAILS-IFREE-SHUTDOWN-BOTH-NODES, H-U6 with
# its census and its window held open.  Run from ~/src/mxfs-e, build
# 1FF993ECCF04A634CC75DD8: the main tree's source (311877C431E1BB444562804's)
# plus, in mxfs_unlprev_rele (xfs/xfs_inode.c), the census counters
# unlprev_rele_inline_last / unlprev_rele_deferred_last, the
# P-UNLPREV-RELE-LAST line, and the test knob dbg_unlprev_rele_hold_ms
# (xfs/xfs_mxfs_dlm.c), all keyed on one condition: the free committed and the
# released reference is the last one on an unlinked predecessor, the only
# release whose irele can run that predecessor's inactivation (the synchronous
# multi-node inactivation in xfs_inode_mark_reclaimable, xfs/xfs_icache.c).
# The harness copy in ~/src/mxfs-e reads the two counters and counts the
# P-UNLPREV-RELE-LAST lines released from a kworker (rele_last_worker).
#
# WHY.  The H-U6 control u6c1 (tests/queues/peer_open_unlinked_hu6_c6.queue)
# did not hang, but its inline arm counted nothing, so it could not show it
# ever reached H-U6's precondition.  hu4df1's cycle needed three things at
# once: the outer free running in a kworker (mxfs_reap_worker), its release
# being the predecessor's last reference (a nested inactivation), and a local
# create taking the outer number before the nested free read the AGI (464 ms
# after the commit, inside the nested free's 600 ms mid-list delay).  The hold
# opens the third for every candidate: 2000 ms between the commit and the
# release, in BOTH arms, so the arms differ only in unlprev_rele_defer.
#
# H-U6 (the record, unchanged): released inline, a last reference on an unlinked
# predecessor runs its inactivation nested inside the outer one after the outer
# free committed; a local create that took the outer number holds the AGI and
# waits in xfs_iget for the outer inode, and the nested free waits for that AGI.
# PREDICTION: the control lap (unlprev_rele_defer=0) hangs with
# rele_inline_last > 0; the fix lap (unlprev_rele_defer=1) completes and PASSes
# with rele_deferred_last > 0.  Under the hold both arms may log P-CR3-NEEDINACT
# (a create waiting for a held inactivation) and that alone is no failure.
#
# Arms, both with dbg_unlprev_rele_hold_ms=2000, dbg_ifree_midlist_delay_ms=600,
# freshsrc_iunl_overlay=1, b6_release_drain=1, unlprev_pin=1, unlprev_tenure=1,
# no close drops, 30 iterations, 2/net/mesh/direct g2c:
#   F  unlprev_rele_defer=1   u6hf1
#   C  unlprev_rele_defer=0   u6hc1, LAST: a hang leaves both nodes wedged
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   VACUOUS (control)  rele_inline_last 0, or rele_last_worker 0: no nested
#             inactivation ran in the context hu4df1's ran in, so a PASS judges
#             nothing.  The control is then rerun with more iterations.
#   VACUOUS (fix)      rele_deferred_last 0.
#   H-U6 SUPPORTED  the control REPRODUCED hung=1, its <node>_dstacks.txt showing
#             xfs_inactive_ifree -> mxfs_unlprev_rele -> xfs_irele -> a nested
#             xfs_inactive -> xfs_inactive_ifree waiting on an AGI buffer lock,
#             and a create in xfs_iget holding it.
#   H-U6 FIXED      with SUPPORTED: the fix lap PASS, hung=0, buflock_stuck=0,
#             rele_deferred_last > 0 and rele_last_worker > 0.  (Two more fix
#             laps and a second control follow before the record is judged
#             FIXED AND VERIFIED; they are a later queue.)
#   H-U6 NOT FIXED  the fix lap hangs or REPRODUCES: attributed from its stacks.
#   H-U6 NOT SUPPORTED HERE  the control PASSes with rele_inline_last > 0 and
#             rele_last_worker > 0: the nested inactivation ran in a kworker
#             with a 2 s hold and nothing deadlocked.  Then the lap's
#             P150-ALLOC-FIN lines are read for a create that took a freed=
#             number inside its hold: none means the window was open but no
#             create used it (rerun with more iterations); one or more means
#             the hypothesis as written is refuted on this build.
# A lap that ABORTs, or audits STALE/NONE without a hang, has no verdict and is
# rerun.
#
# Bound per lap: tests/queues/peer_open_unlinked_hu6_ab.queue's 2397 s plus the
# seventh PUC_KNOBS knob, 2 x 20 = 2437 s.  The holds sit inside the harness's
# own workload bound (30 x 11 + 60 = 390 s): the fix laps of that queue ran
# 300 s per lap end to end, and a hold delays only a free's tail.
2437 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_KNOBS="freshsrc_iunl_overlay=1 b6_release_drain=1 unlprev_pin=1 dbg_ifree_midlist_delay_ms=600 unlprev_tenure=1 unlprev_rele_defer=1 dbg_unlprev_rele_hold_ms=2000" tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh u6hf1 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
2437 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_KNOBS="freshsrc_iunl_overlay=1 b6_release_drain=1 unlprev_pin=1 dbg_ifree_midlist_delay_ms=600 unlprev_tenure=1 unlprev_rele_defer=0 dbg_unlprev_rele_hold_ms=2000" tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh u6hc1 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
